
                                 OPERATORS
                                 =========

Numeric
-------
Most of these are standard to all versions of BASIC except for the bitwise
operators which a lot of BASICs don't support or use different operators.

  +   plus
  -   minus
  *   multiply
  /   divide
  %   modulus
  ^   power

  &   bitwise AND
  |   bitwise OR
  !   bitwise XOR (! because ^ is BASIC standard for power)
  <<  bitwise shift left
  >>  bitwise shift right

  =   equals
  <   less than
  >   greater than
  >=  greater than or equals
  <=  less than or equals
  <>  not equal
  
  AND logical AND
  OR  logical OR
  XOR logical XOR

  (   left bracket
  )   right bracket

eg: print (5 << 1) * 2 & 7

String
------
The string comparison operators simply call the C lib strcmp function.

  &   concatenate

  =   equals
  <   less than
  >   greater than
  >=  greater than or equals
  <=  less than or equals
  <>  not equal
  
  (   left bracket
  )   right bracket

eg: print "de" & "f" > "abc"

You can also mix string and numeric operations as long as you use brackets.

eg: result = ("def" > "abc") * 10

